+## Memory lifecycle and team conflicts
+
+Every decision about a project's memory (created, edited, forgotten, restored, pinned, merged, archived) is a line of a plain journal kept in the shared brain, with its author (you, an agent, the sync, the learning loop) and its reason; each memory has its own history.
+
+- **Forget** puts the note in a trash for 30 days, from which **Restore** puts it back (with a warning if it contradicts a current memory).
+- **Pin** (50 per project) protects a memory from any automatic removal.
+- The **Lifecycle** tab of Context shows the journal; the Memories tab has the actions on each memory.
+- A note brought by a team sync that contradicts a note of the project (« always » against « never », two values for the same setting, opposite recommendations) is detected without a model, offline. Safe cases settle themselves (the pinned note, the safer pattern or the much more recent note wins); the others wait side by side until you keep one, write the canonical note or say it is not a conflict. A model can give its opinion on request, never decide.
+
+Design: [memory-lifecycle.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/memory-lifecycle.md).
+
