+## REA: what a shipped build exposes
+
+[REA](https://github.com/morluto/rea) (npm `rea-agents`) reads a build without running it. WorkPilot pins one version (installed in one click from **CLI Tools**) and runs only its static readers, without a shell or your credentials.
+
+- **Artifact exposure gate** — after QA, REA reads the build output the task left (Electron or Tauri bundle, APK, web build and its source maps, .NET `publish` folder, jar, wheel, Rust binary…) and reports what it exposes. It warns by default; in `strict`, or when the workflow declares the hard gate `artifact-exposure`, an exposed check at the threshold sends the task back to the fixer. The Release Train runs the same `exposure` step before deploying each service.
+- **Public .NET API kept during a migration** — after QA on a .NET task, each library it touches is built before and after the task in throwaway copies and REA compares the two assemblies: a public member removed, made internal, renamed or with a changed signature is reported. It blocks during a .NET migration prepared by WorkPilot, or when the workflow declares `public-api-stable`.
+- What REA could not decide never blocks, and a check that could not run never counts as passed. Design: [rea.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/rea.md).
+
+## WinDev, WebDev and WinDev Mobile
+
+A project saved in text format (Git option, version 25 and later) gets the `wlangage` and `windev-text-format` skills, and every Kanban agent knows it edits only WLangage code, never the properties only the editor writes nor binary files; what only the editor can do becomes a « To do in the WinDev editor » step. A QA gate compares each changed WinDev file with its version before the task and sends back anything only the editor may write (a binary changed, an invented control or element, a duplicated `procedure_id`, a file that no longer reads). WLangage is coloured in the diff viewer and can be translated to other languages; a project in native format is reported instead of guessed, and compiling and testing stay in WinDev. Design: [windev.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/windev.md).
